      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A 10 nm NiO layer will be deposited on the alloy by room-temperature reactive sputtering.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "NiO is antiferromagnetic under the proposed conditions.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant blocking temperature of the 10 nm NiO layer is approximately 250°C.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Field cooling the NiO-coated alloy from above to below the NiO blocking temperature will induce exchange bias.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Exchange coupling at the NiO/CoCrFeMnNi interface will pin magnetic domain walls.",
